<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tales of the Alhambra</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1832</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tales of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alhambra">Alhambra</a> is a collection of essays, sketches and legends by the American writer Washington Irving, published in 1832 after he had lived in the Alhambra palace in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/granada">Granada</a> in 1829. Mixing descriptions of the palace and its inhabitants with Moorish legends, it made the Alhambra famous among European and American readers and fed Romantic interest in Islamic <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tales-of-the-alhambra.jpg" alt="Tales of the Alhambra" width="320" height="510" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Washington Irving · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_Alhambra,_London_1832,_title-page.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
